.TH MKFN 1
.SH NAME
mkfn \- describe a font for troff
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mkfn
[
.B -a
|
.B -o
] [
.B -s
] [
.B -b
] [
.B -l
] [
.B -n
] [
.B -g
] [
.B -w
] [
.B -c
] [
.B -M
] [
.BI -p " name"
] [
.BI -t " name"
] [
.BI -f " path"
] [
.BI -r " res"
] [
.BI -k " kmin"
] [
.BI -S " scripts"
] [
.BI -L " languages"
] [
.BI -F " font"
] [
.I font
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Mkfn
writes the description
.IR troff (1)
sets a font by: its glyphs, their widths and bounding boxes, the
characters each is, and its OpenType substitutions and positionings
(ligatures, small capitals, kerning and the rest), from an OpenType,
TrueType or AFM font.
It is a translation of Ali Gholami Rudi's Neatmkfn;
.B /lib/troff/devutf/mkdesc
makes the device's descriptions with it.
.PP
Without
.BR -c ,
it differs from Neatmkfn where troff is better served: a CFF glyph's
bounding box is read from its outline; an alias does not take a
character the font has its own glyph for; a lookup the font's scripts
share is written once, not once for each (troff would perform each
copy); and a pair kerning subtable's first class 0 is every glyph of
its coverage given no other class.
.TP
.B -a
.TP
.B -o
The font is AFM (the default), or OpenType or TrueType.
.TP
.B -s
A special font: searched for a character the current font lacks.
.TP
.BI -p " name"
.TP
.BI -t " name"
.TP
.BI -f " path"
Its PostScript name, troff's name for it, and its file.
.TP
.BI -r " res"
The device's resolution (720).
.TP
.BI -k " kmin"
The least kerning written (0).
.TP
.B -b
Each glyph's bounding box.
.TP
.B -l
No ligatures line.
.TP
.B -n
No glyph positions.
.TP
.B -g
Glyphs by name in the rules.
.TP
.BI -S " scripts"
.TP
.BI -L " languages"
The scripts and languages kept, apart by commas
.RB ( list
lists them).
.TP
.BI -F " font"
A font of a collection.
.TP
.B -w
Say what of the font is not supported.
.TP
.B -c
Write as Neatmkfn writes.
.TP
.B -M
Write not the font's description but its MATH table (an OpenType math
font's), as
.IR eqn (1)'s
settings for it, mounted as the font
.B -t
names (S): its constants; its maths italic letters' glyphs
.RB ( mathital ),
italic corrections
.RB ( italcorr )
and top accent attachments
.RB ( accentpos );
its accents and their wider variants
.RB ( accent );
its delimiters' and radical's sizes, their heights and pieces
.RB ( bracketsizes ,
.BR bracketheights ,
.BR bracketpieces );
its braces' over and under
.RB ( bracesizes ,
.BR bracepieces );
its big operators, each its display size and italic correction, and the
symbols eqnrc names
.RB ( define ).
.B /lib/troff/eqnrc
holds what it writes for Libertinus Math; for another math font, put
what it writes for that one there instead:
.IP
.EX
mkfn -b -l -o -s -r7200 -tS -f/fonts/lm/latinmodern-math.otf /fonts/lm/latinmodern-math.otf >S
mkfn -M /fonts/lm/latinmodern-math.otf >math.rc
.EE
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/mkfn
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR troff (1),
.IR tr2pdf (1)
